  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">-  Improved coordination between integrity institutions and stakeholders delivering the National Anti-Corruption Strategy
- Increased proportion of press articles referring to reports and communication by integrity institutions and coordination mechanisms.
-  Increased [confidence in] knowledge and capacity to deliver results in their job of staff working on integrity prevention and investigation in integrity institutions
-  Increased capacity of implementing parties identified in the NACS to deliver results according to NACS Action Plan
-  Increased capacity of NACS implementing parties and integrity institutions to prevent leakages linked to corruption
-  SiIncreased capacity of civil society and private sector to hold institutions accountable in line with the National Anti-Corruption Strategymplified systems are in place to reduce opportunity for corruption in institutional processes and access to services
-  Increased self-evaluation of empowerment and ability to fight corruption amongst students in Solomon Islands</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Initiate the Community Outreach Program within 6 village communities around Isabel Province together with Anti Corruption Secretariat, Office of Prime Minister &amp; Cabinet, Isabel Provincial Government, Solomon Islands Independent Commission Against Corruption (SIICAC), Leadership Code Commission (LCC), Office of the Director of Public Prosecutions (ODPP), Ombudsman Office. Highlight the importance of the Anti Corruption Act 2018, Whistle Blowers Act, SIICACs roles and functions and mark the International Anti Corruption Day 2021.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Achieved a successful community outreach around Isabel Province reaching 300 students, and in addition reached more than 8 village communities to raise awareness on the Anti Corruption Act 2018, Whistle Blowers Act and to inform Communities on the roles and function of the Solomon Islands Independent Commission Against Corruption (SIICAC) based on the Anti Corruption Act 2018. The community outreach was summed up with the International Anti Corruption Day 2021 event that took place in Buala, Isabel Province. The whole outreach and final event was done in partnership with Isabel Provincial Government, and representatives from key Integrity Institutions; Leadership Code Commission (LCC), Office of the Director of Public Prosecutions (ODPP), and the Ombudsman Office together with the Anti Corruption Secretariat, Office of Prime Minister &amp; Cabinet and UNDP TAP Project</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Finalization of the Rights to Information Bill (drafting) and its passage in Parliament.
- Support operationalisation of SIICAC and drafting of SOP procedures
- Partnership with civil society and youth organisations for awareness and advocacy work on fight against corruption.
- Pilot initiative and scale-up activities for fight against corruption
-Support government and civil society on Anti-corruption international day celebrations</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
